# Compliance and security audit

TORN Daily Resource Tracker 1.0.0. Audit date: 2 October 2026.
Scope: `torn-daily-resource-tracker.user.js`, the exact file delivered.

## 1. Sources checked

* **Torn API documentation** (`https://www.torn.com/api.html`):
  * the API is read-only;
  * 100 requests per minute per user, across all keys;
  * how the ToS table must be shown;
  * error codes;
  * the 30-second service cache and the `timestamp` parameter that bypasses it;
  * the `comment` parameter;
  * repeated requests with invalid keys can trigger temporary IP blocks.
* **Torn API v2 OpenAPI spec 6.13.4** (September 2026). Every endpoint, selection, stat name and response field the script reads was checked against it, including the access level each one needs.
* **Torn wiki:**
  * City: maximum 100 items per day from East Side shops.
  * Casino: 75 tokens at New Day.
  * Points: each refill once per day, resetting at New Day.
  * Organized Crime 2.0: every member must be in Torn and not hospitalized when the crime starts.
  * Travel: 3% flight variance; travel times changed in June 2026.
  * Activity Log.
* **Torn's scripting rule**, as publicly quoted. Scripts may only use API data or data from a page the user loaded manually and is viewing. They may not make extra non-API requests, scrape pages that are not being viewed, or bypass the CAPTCHA.
* **Not loaded directly:** `https://www.torn.com/rules.php` blocks automated access. Read it yourself before publishing (see section 9).

## 2. Network endpoints (complete list)

| # | Request | Purpose | Key access | When |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `GET https://api.torn.com/v2/key/info` | Learn the key's access level and allowed selections, so only permitted data is requested | Any key | At start, after a key change, every 6 h |
| 2 | `GET https://api.torn.com/v2/user?selections=bars,cooldowns,refills,travel,organizedcrime,timestamp[,casino]&legacy=refills&timestamp=<now>` | Live data and Torn server time (see notes below the table) | Minimal (Limited for casino) | Every 30, 60 or 120 s (60 s default); New Day +3 s and +35 s; manual refresh at most once per 10 s |
| 3 | `GET https://api.torn.com/v2/user/personalstats?stat=xantaken,cityitemsbought,refills,nerverefills,tokenrefills` | Counters for Xanax, City Shop and refill confirmation | Public or higher | Every 2 min |
| 4 | Same as #3 with `&timestamp=<00:00 TCT minus 1 s>` | Torn's historical value as the New Day baseline | Public or higher | Only when needed, at most 3 per day |
| 5 | `GET https://api.torn.com/v2/user/log?from=&to=&limit=100` | Activity log for the energy and nerve breakdown, and confirmation of Xanax and City Shop | Full, or custom with `log` | Every 2 min, only new entries; at most 15 pages per pass; yesterday's last minutes once more after New Day |

Notes on request #2:
* `casino` is only requested with a Limited or higher key.
* `legacy=refills` asks for the explicit `*_refill_used` fields.
* The `timestamp` query parameter bypasses Torn's 30-second cache.

How every request is sent:
* Method GET, with browser credentials omitted.
* Tagged `comment=TRTracker`.
* One queue: at most 20 requests per minute, duplicates merged while in flight, 15-second timeout.
* Retries with backoff for network or backend errors only.
* Only one Torn tab sends requests; the others read the shared results.

Typical steady load: about 1.5 requests per minute with a Limited key and about 2 with a Full key. Hidden tabs poll three times slower.

**Links**, opened only when you click them, in a new tab with `noopener noreferrer`:
* The author's profile (support message).
* Torn's API key settings page.

**Nothing else:** no remote scripts, fonts, images, analytics, telemetry, proxies or third-party servers.

## 3. Page data

* **Travel page only** (`travelagency.php` or `page.php?sid=travel`), while you are viewing it. The script reads the `data-model` attribute of `#travel-root` and the checked travel type and destination inputs. It is read-only, and the MutationObserver only watches that element.
* **Theme:** reads the `dark-mode` class on Torn's `body`.
* **DOM changes:** the script adds one `<style id="trt-style">` and one `<div id="trt-root">`. Torn's own elements are never modified, hidden, clicked or blocked.

